# Read ONE sensor, on demand. Replaces the 20 is_sensor_*() calls.
#
# This is the faithful mapping of the HTTP behaviour: over HTTP the GUI read a
# sensor only when it needed that sensor, so the serial port saw traffic only on
# demand. AxisSensors.msg (the periodic topic) is the nicer interface, but it
# polls all 20 sensors on a timer, which puts continuous traffic on the very
# serial ports the motion commands share. On this rig that is exactly the
# interleaving that axis_module_yuanman warns about, so the topic is opt-in and
# this service is the default path.
#
# name is the is_sensor_* method name without the prefix:
#   x_left     x_org     x_right     x_move
#   y_down     y_org     y_up        y_move
#   z_back     z_org     z_forward   z_move
#   yaw_left   yaw_org   yaw_right   yaw_move
#   pitch_down pitch_org pitch_up    pitch_move
string name
---
bool success

# The value the module returned. A serial error makes the module return None,
# which HTTP delivered as null and the client treated as falsy; here that
# becomes False and success is set to false so the caller can tell them apart.
bool value
string message
